{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "fc", "rep": 223, "hyps": [{"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Raising an already large Adam step size causes divergence and collapsing accuracy, unlike at small or moderate rates."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "higher", "why": "At tiny learning rates the network is undertrained in 243 epochs, so increasing the rate gives large gains (e.g. +29pp on vehicle)."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "depth", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deeper ReLU nets are less stable, so a larger step size hurts more (exp 10 vs 9)."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "width", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Very wide layers amplify effective update magnitude, so raising the learning rate is more damaging (exp 14 vs 13)."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "down", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "higher", "why": "Lowering a divergent learning rate recovers training, giving large gains that do not occur at small rates."}, {"edit_param": "alpha", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "alpha", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Once the L2 penalty is strong, increasing it further causes underfitting and clear accuracy drops, whereas at tiny alpha it is negligible."}, {"edit_param": "alpha", "edit_dir": "down", "cond_param": "alpha", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "higher", "why": "Relaxing an overly strong L2 penalty restores model capacity (exp 99, 100), while at small alpha it has no effect."}, {"edit_param": "batch_size", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "higher", "why": "Larger batches reduce gradient noise and stabilize training at high learning rates (exp 23, 26)."}, {"edit_param": "depth", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Adding layers at high learning rates triggers instability and collapse (exp 59, 62)."}, {"edit_param": "width", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Widening the net at high learning rates worsens instability (exp 44, 50), while at moderate rates width changes are near-neutral."}], "tok": 27162, "bad": 0, "probes": [[[3, 0, 1, 0, 3], 3, "up"], [[3, 9, 1, 0, 3], 3, "up"], [[3, 0, 1, 4, 3], 3, "up"], [[3, 9, 1, 4, 3], 3, "up"], [[3, 0, 1, 7, 3], 3, "up"], [[3, 9, 1, 7, 3], 3, "up"], [[3, 4, 0, 4, 3], 3, "up"], [[3, 4, 2, 4, 3], 3, "up"], [[3, 4, 0, 6, 3], 3, "up"], [[3, 4, 2, 6, 3], 3, "up"], [[3, 4, 1, 4, 0], 3, "up"], [[3, 4, 1, 4, 9], 3, "up"], [[3, 4, 1, 6, 0], 3, "up"], [[3, 4, 1, 6, 9], 3, "up"], [[3, 9, 1, 2, 0], 3, "up"], [[3, 0, 1, 2, 9], 3, "up"], [[9, 4, 1, 5, 3], 3, "up"], [[0, 4, 1, 5, 3], 3, "up"], [[3, 9, 2, 1, 3], 3, "up"], [[3, 0, 0, 1, 3], 3, "up"], [[3, 1, 1, 0, 3], 1, "up"], [[3, 1, 1, 4, 3], 1, "up"], [[3, 1, 1, 7, 3], 1, "up"], [[3, 7, 1, 0, 3], 1, "up"], [[3, 7, 1, 4, 3], 1, "up"], [[3, 7, 1, 7, 3], 1, "up"], [[3, 4, 0, 4, 3], 1, "up"], [[3, 4, 2, 4, 3], 1, "up"], [[3, 4, 1, 4, 0], 1, "up"], [[3, 4, 1, 4, 9], 1, "up"], [[9, 4, 1, 4, 3], 1, "up"], [[0, 4, 1, 4, 3], 1, "up"], [[3, 2, 2, 2, 3], 1, "up"], [[3, 8, 0, 6, 3], 1, "up"], [[3, 5, 1, 8, 3], 1, "up"], [[3, 5, 1, 1, 3], 1, "up"], [[3, 4, 0, 4, 0], 4, "up"], [[3, 4, 2, 4, 0], 4, "up"], [[3, 4, 0, 4, 4], 4, "up"], [[3, 4, 2, 4, 4], 4, "up"], [[3, 4, 0, 4, 7], 4, "up"], [[3, 4, 2, 4, 7], 4, "up"], [[3, 4, 1, 0, 3], 4, "up"], [[3, 4, 1, 7, 3], 4, "up"], [[9, 4, 1, 4, 3], 4, "up"], [[0, 4, 1, 4, 3], 4, "up"], [[3, 0, 1, 4, 3], 4, "up"], [[3, 9, 1, 4, 3], 4, "up"], [[3, 4, 1, 6, 1], 4, "up"], [[3, 4, 1, 6, 8], 4, "up"], [[3, 4, 1, 1, 1], 4, "up"], [[3,